\label{krull-domain-defn}


An integral domain $A$ is called a \emph{Krull domain}
if it satisfies the following properties:
\begin{itemize}
\item
$A_{\mathfrak{p}}$ is a discrete valuation ring for all height one primes ${\mathfrak{p}}$ of $A$,
\item
$A=\bigcap_{{\mathfrak{p}}\in{\mathrm{Spec}}(A),{\mathrm{ht}}({\mathfrak{p}})=1}A_{\mathfrak{p}}$ inside ${\mathrm{Frac}}(A)$,
\item
any nonzero element of $A$ is contained in only a finitely many height one primes of $A$.
\end{itemize}

\label{ht-1-localization-is-PID}


A Noetherian ring $A$ is called
``height one localizations are PID'', if
for any finitely many height one primes ${\mathfrak{p}}_1,\cdots,{\mathfrak{p}}_r$ ($r\geq 1$) of $A$,
let $S:=A\setminus\bigcup_{i=1}^r{\mathfrak{p}}_i$, then $S^{-1}A$ is a PID.

